      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE",
          "content": "This article describes development and evaluation of a 4-scenario instrument designed to measure reasoning abilities for managing asthma symptoms."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Existing literature informed creation of a reasoning template and the reasoning scenarios. Think-aloud interviews appraised scenario functionality. Experts assessed content validity. Data from 2 groups of students with asthma aged 9-15 years (N = 132 and 307) were used to evaluate psychometric properties."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The scenarios were deemed functional, content was relevant, and readability was age/grade appropriate. Cronbach's alpha was 0.79. Exploratory and confirmatory factor analyses indicated a single component solution and revealed a good fit. Concurrent validity was established using correlations with asthma knowledge."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The instrument could be used to assess reasoning about symptom management and to evaluate educational interventions."
        }
      ]},
